.TH CLEAN-MINES 6 "2026-07-02" "clean-mines 0.1.0" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
clean-mines \- tiny native Minesweeper game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clean-mines
[\fB--graphics\fR]
[\fB--terminal\fR]
[\fB--commands\fR]
[\fB--dark\fR]
[\fB--light\fR]
[\fB--theme\fR \fIlight|dark\fR]
[\fB--level\fR \fIsmall|medium|large\fR]
[\fB--difficulty\fR \fIeasy|normal|hard\fR]
[\fB--width\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--height\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--mines\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--seed\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B clean-mines
\fB--self-test\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clean-mines
is a tiny native Minesweeper game with graphical and terminal modes.
The default mode is graphical when SDL2 support is built in.
Graphical mode uses the dark theme by default and fixed 32x32 tile cells.
Terminal mode uses a full-screen arrow-key controller when stdin and stdout are TTYs.
Line-command terminal mode is used automatically for pipes and can be forced with
.B --commands.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --graphics
Run graphical mode.
.TP
.B --terminal
Run terminal mode.
.TP
.B --commands
Use line-command terminal mode.
.TP
.B --dark
Use the dark graphical theme. This is the graphical default.
.TP
.B --light
Use the light graphical theme.
.TP
.BI --theme " light|dark"
Set the graphical theme.
.TP
.BI --level " small|medium|large"
Set the preset board size level.
.TP
.BI --difficulty " easy|normal|hard"
Set the preset mine difficulty within the size level.
.TP
.BI --width " N"
Set the board width.
.TP
.BI --height " N"
Set the board height.
.TP
.BI --mines " N"
Set the mine count.
.TP
.BI --seed " N"
Use a deterministic random seed.
.TP
.B --self-test
Run built-in engine tests.
.TP
.B --help
Show command help.
.TP
.B --version
Show the program version.
.SH CONTROLS
Graphical mode supports left click or Space/Enter to reveal, right click or
.B f
to flag, arrow keys to move keyboard focus,
.B Tab
or
.B o
to open the graphical menu for size, difficulty, theme, flag mode, and reset,
.B t
to toggle light and dark themes,
.B 1/s/b
to select small size,
.B 2/m/i
to select medium size,
.B 3/l/x
to select large size,
.B e/n/h
to select easy, normal, or hard difficulty,
.B r
to restart, and
.B q
or Escape to quit.
.PP
Full-screen terminal mode supports arrow keys to move the flashing focused cell,
Space/Enter to reveal,
.B f
to flag,
.B c
to chord,
.B r
to restart,
.B ?
to toggle help, and
.B q
or Escape to quit.
.PP
Line-command terminal mode supports:
.TP
.BI r " x y"
Reveal a cell.
.TP
.BI f " x y"
Flag or unflag a cell.
.TP
.BI c " x y"
Chord a revealed numbered cell.
.TP
.B n
Restart the current board.
.TP
.BI n " s h"
Start a new board by size level and difficulty.
.TP
.BI s " m"
Select a size level while keeping the current difficulty.
.TP
.BI d " e"
Select a difficulty while keeping the current size level.
.TP
.B n b
Start a small normal board.
.TP
.B n i
Start a medium normal board.
.TP
.B n e
Start a large normal board.
.TP
.B h
Show in-game help.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH AUTHOR
RaresKeY
